<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - TGS cut to hold.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - TGS cut to hold.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Morgan Grenfell analyst Carlos de Leon cut his rating for Argentina's Transportadora de Gas del Sur SA, or TGS, Thursday to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- In a report, he said he was reducing the rating &quot;in view of the expected tariff review on 28 June, at which we expect the regulator Enargas to reduce current transport tariffs.&quot;</p>
<p>-- &quot;... The stock has underperformed the market by 4.3 percent over the past three months.&quot;</p>
<p>-- American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) in TGS opened down 1/8 to 12-3/4.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
